# Sync `production` Branch

This repo has a lean orphan branch **`production`** (Compose deploy tree only).

Whenever you change anything on **`main`** that also belongs on **`production`**, update **`production` in the same turn** — do not wait to be asked.

## What lives on `production`

- `docker-compose.yml` (image pull only; no `build:`)
- `example.env`
- `init.sh`
- `README.md` (deploy-focused)
- `configs/traefik/traefik.base.yml`
- Empty runtime dirs with `.gitkeep` (`data/…`, `logs/…`, `configs/traefik/vhosts/`)
- `.gitignore`, `LICENSE`

## Always mirror when you touch

| Change on `main` | Action on `production` |
|------------------|------------------------|
| `example.env` | Copy / apply the same env keys & comments |
| `docker-compose.yml` (runtime/ports/volumes/env) | Apply equivalent changes; **never** add a local `build:` section |
| `scripts/init.sh` or init behavior | Update `init.sh` on `production` |
| Traefik base static config | Update `configs/traefik/traefik.base.yml` |
| Quick start / deploy docs in root `README.md` | Keep `production` README deploy steps accurate |
| App version / default `TPM_IMAGE` tag | Align version comments / image tag defaults if present |
| New required data/log dirs | Add dirs + `.gitkeep` on `production` |

## Do not copy onto `production`

Source code (`server/`, `web/`), `Dockerfile`, `.github/`, `docs/`, `images/`, `Makefile`, tests, `node_modules`, etc.

## How to apply

1. Finish the `main` edit.
2. Check out or patch `production` (worktree / checkout) and apply the mirrored files.
3. Leave commits/pushes to the user unless they explicitly ask to commit or push.

If a change is deploy-relevant and you only updated `main`, that is incomplete work.
